-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version] 5755-1995, s 334(a)(1): WHICH RISE OF THE INDEX it takes for the reduced collection threshold.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt
-- by tools/srcquote.py.
--
-- This module supplies the INPUT row IL-04's nii-s334-interpretation.l4 takes (the two readings, or the rate): it does not update the
-- threshold, and does not round (s 334 states no rounding; the 2026 figure the text prints is 7,703). It returns the signed rate
-- of rise; a fall is a negative rate (IL-04's fork F6 is what a fall does).
--
-- THE INDEX. NII s 1 defines "the index" as the consumer price index the Bureau publishes monthly (quoted next). Unlike the Ordinance
-- s 1, the National Insurance Law s 1 does not define "the rate of rise of the index"; s 334(a)(1) names the two readings itself, so no
-- definition is borrowed from the Ordinance.
-- src:171 | ”מדד“ – מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת מדי חודש הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה;

§ `Section 334(a)(1) — the rise of the index`

-- src:3605 | ”מדרגת גבייה מופחתת“ – סכום של 7,522 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2025; בשנת 2026, 7,703 ש״ח)], כשהוא מעודכן ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה כלהלן:
-- src:3606 | (1) בשנים 2026 עד 2028 – לפי שיעור עליית המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני 1 בינואר, לעומת המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני 1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת;
-- "according to the rate of rise of the index published last before 1 January, against the index published last before 1 January of the
-- previous year", in the years 2026 to 2028. For 1 January Y: the reading published last before 1 January Y (November of Y-1) against the
-- reading published last before 1 January Y-1 (November of Y-2). From 2029 (2) uses the average wage, not the index; before 2026 the text
-- does not apply (the threshold is printed for 2025).
@ref NII s 334(a)(1) (source line 3606), s 1 "מדד" (source line 171); fork F1
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      how        IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a)(1) — the rate of rise of the index for 1 January of` `the year` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2026 AND `the year` AT MOST 2028
    THEN `the rate of rise of the index from`
             (`the reading last published before the start of` (`the calendar month in year` (`the year` MINUS 1) `, number` 1))
             `to`
             (`the reading last published before the start of` (`the calendar month in year` `the year` `, number` 1))
             `, comparing readings of two bases as` how
    ELSE `section 334(a)(1) takes the rise of the index only for 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028`

@ref NII s 334(a)(1) (source line 3606); fork F1
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a)(1) — the rate of rise of the index for 1 January of` `the year` MEANS
    `s 334(a)(1) — the rate of rise of the index for 1 January of` `the year`
        `, comparing readings of two bases as` `section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases`

@ref NII s 334(a)(1)-(2) (source lines 3606-3607)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 334(a)(1) takes the rise of the index only for 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 334(a)(1) takes the rise of the index only for 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028; from 2029 clause (2) uses the average wage, and before 2026 the text in the sources does not apply"

-- The two readings as numbers on one scale, in the shape IL-04's rule takes them (same field names as IL-03's `Index readings for a period`).
@ref NII s 334(a)(1) (source line 3606); fork F1
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Index readings on one scale for a period`
`s 334(a)(1) — the readings for 1 January of` `the year` MEANS
    IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2026 AND `the year` AT MOST 2028
    THEN `the readings on one scale for`
             (`A period of whole months`
                 WITH `the first month of the period` IS `the calendar month in year` (`the year` MINUS 1) `, number` 1
                 ,    `the last month of the period`  IS `the calendar month in year` (`the year` MINUS 1) `, number` 12)
    ELSE `section 334(a)(1) takes the rise of the index only for 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028`
